# PRs and git

- Branch per task: `agent/<short-task>`. Small PRs, one intent, < ~400 changed lines when possible.
- Conventional titles: `feat|fix|test|docs|refactor|chore|perf(scope): summary`.
- PR body sections (required): What · Why · How verified (exact commands + trimmed output) · Numbers changed (before → after + command) · Risks · Not done / follow-ups · Plan link (`.cursor/plans/...`) · Agent run link if any.
- Attach artifacts for anything visual or behavioral (screenshot, short video, eval table).
- Never force-push shared branches, rewrite history, tag, or publish. A human merges.
- The shell guard matches `git pull` and denies rebasing pulls (`git pull --rebase`, `git pull -r`). A plain `git pull` is allowed. It denies force-push and `reset --hard` wherever the flag sits (`git push origin --force`, `git push origin -f`, `git reset HEAD --hard`), plus tags, publish commands, and a missing, blank, or non-string command. Invalid JSON fails closed. A plain `git push` asks.
- Package releases are `pypi-v<version>` only. Action releases stay `v1.x`. Use `.claude/skills/release/SKILL.md`. Do not tag or publish from an agent.
- Address every Bugbot finding: fix it or reply with a reason. Don't silently resolve.
